  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5751e45b3bc551448917ed569792a2a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: About the mission
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  fullText: "project NAME\n\nFirst proposed in 2035, and officially beginning in
    2046, project NAME was humanity's most ambitious attempt to explore the universe.\nDivided
    into four different phases, it carefully laid foundations, defined requirements,
    detailed steps, and set realistic objectives needed \nto reach planets far beyond
    our solar system.\n\nPhase one required a monumental technological jump, as every
    scientist around the world gathered to figure out the fastest and most \nefficient
    way to travel through space. Simultaneously, mass industrialization was set in
    motion to prepare the production of soon-to-be \nneeded satellites, starships,
    space platforms, and more.\n\nAfter years of progress and unparalleled breakthroughs,
    phase two began in 2062, when the first unmanned mission to test faster-than-\nlight
    travel was initiated. Many failures followed, as humanity adapted, improved,
    and eventually overcame the complex task of traveling \nquickly and safely.\n\nThe
    year 2087 marks the start of phase three: the first expedition with a crew set
    to visit and analyze several solar systems where life \ncould be sustainable.
    The most advanced spacecraft to date, NAME, currently carries 20 volunteers towards
    every promising star, where \nthey will scan suitable planets in hopes of finding
    water existing in a liquid state, as well as a breathable atmosphere.\n\nWe find
    ourselves awaiting for news, while we continue to prepare for the hopefully inevitable
    day in which we move into phase four: \nthe large scale migration to a new world."
